# tally 2.2.1 R18 (L §4.3: a move binds its keys in the order written; a read that states its own day needs no law
# date; the engine's move_read_dated):
# 235.8: "a pin changes none of this": (act_day as if {act_day = dpin}) in a key's on before the at is
# LOAD-LAWDATE (review-probes/gatefix/p/o_pin_at.d). tally 2.2: run answered with the pin.
=== options exit=1
=== o_pin_at.d.tally
model m
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-01-31

source s "s"

unit PLN: currency minor 0.01

place konto: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..
place spare: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..2026-01-20
place shop: outside lives 1900-01-01..

index wk = day 2026-01-05..2026-01-11

input fee: money PLN
input cal: calendar
input act_day: date
input gap: date
input n: int
input d0: date
input dfix: date
input dpin: date

band lim(x: int): int

def rd: date = act_day at reader
def rd2: date = rd at reader
def own: date = act_day at dfix
def owndated: date = act_day at gap
def nb: date = add_business(d0, 1, cal)

move shut[p in accounts on (act_day as if {act_day = dpin})]: transfers
  on d0
  at lifespan(p).to
  leg cash from p to shop amount fee

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  fee = 10.00 PLN
  d0 = 2026-01-09
  dfix = 2026-01-01
  dpin = 2026-01-07
  opening[konto] = 100.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "w"
  opening[spare] = 100.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "w"

version c
  cite s
  governs 2026..
  known 2026-01-01
  cal = calendar(weekends [sat, sun])
  act_day = 2026-01-08
  gap = 2026-01-02
  n = 2
  lim: [0, inf) = 2

ask q: bal(konto, 2026-01-31)
ask q2: bal(spare, 2026-01-19)
=== expect
refused: LOAD-LAWDATE move shut's key p reads law-dated act_day with no law date: its at reads p (o_pin_at.d.tally:34)
